---
/**
 * Terms of service.
 *
 * Deliberately short, because this site does very little: it has no accounts,
 * sells nothing, and takes no payments. Clauses about user accounts,
 * subscriptions, refunds or arbitration would be copied from a template for a
 * different kind of site and would not describe anything real here.
 *
 * If the site ever does take payments or create accounts, this page needs
 * rewriting rather than extending.
 */
import Navbar from '../components/home/navbar.jsx';
import Footer from '../components/home/footer.jsx';
import '../components/css/pages.css';

const updated = 'October 19, 2026';
const email = 'jchsfbla@gmail.com';
---

<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <title>Terms of Service | Johns Creek FBLA</title>
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <meta name="description" content="Terms for using the Johns Creek FBLA chapter website." />
  <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css?family=Oswald&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
  <style>
    html, body { margin: 0; padding: 0; background-color: #f7f7f7; font-family: 'Oswald', sans-serif; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <Navbar client:load />
  <main class="page legal">
    <header class="page-heading">
      <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
      <p class="page-intro">
        Last updated {updated}. Short, because this site does not do much: there
        is nothing to sign up for and nothing for sale.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="panel">
      <div class="panel-header"><h2>What this site is</h2></div>
      <p class="panel-body">
        An information site for Johns Creek FBLA, the student chapter at Johns
        Creek High School, maintained by chapter officers. It is student-run. It
        is not an official publication of Fulton County Schools or of FBLA, and
        nothing posted here changes school, district, or FBLA policy.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="panel">
      <div class="panel-header"><h2>Accuracy</h2></div>
      <p class="panel-body">
        We keep dates, prices and deadlines as current as we can, and they do
        change, sometimes with little notice. Where this site disagrees with the
        chapter advisor, Georgia FBLA, or Fulton County Schools, they are right
        and we are out of date. Before you pay for a trip or travel to an event,
        confirm it with an officer or with the advisor.
      </p>
      <p class="panel-body">
        Spotted something wrong? Tell us at <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a> and
        we will fix it.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="panel">
      <div class="panel-header"><h2>No accounts, nothing for sale</h2></div>
      <p class="panel-body">
        There is no account to create here and nothing is sold on this site.
        Forms are hosted by Google or Microsoft. Payments happen on Fulton
        County Schools' SchoolCash Online. Those services carry their own terms,
        and using them means agreeing to theirs as well as to this page.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="panel">
      <div class="panel-header"><h2>Using our words and photos</h2></div>
      <p class="panel-body">
        Text and photos here were made by chapter members for the chapter. Using
        them for school or FBLA purposes is fine, and a credit is appreciated.
        Two limits: do not use photos of students commercially, and do not use
        them in a way the person in the photo would object to. If you are
        unsure, ask at <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>.
      </p>
      <p class="panel-body">
        The FBLA name and emblem belong to FBLA. We use them as a member
        chapter, which does not give anyone else permission through us.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="panel">
      <div class="panel-header"><h2>Using the site</h2></div>
      <p class="panel-body">
        Read it, share it, link to it. Do not try to break it, overload it, or
        deface it, and do not use it to harass anyone.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="panel">
      <div class="panel-header"><h2>Links we do not control</h2></div>
      <p class="panel-body">
        We link to Georgia FBLA, FBLA, Instagram, Linktree, Snap! Raise,
        SchoolCash Online and Google documents. We do not run those sites and
        cannot vouch for them, and a link is not an endorsement.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="panel">
      <div class="panel-header"><h2>What we can and cannot promise</h2></div>
      <p class="panel-body">
        Students build and run this site in their own time, and it costs nothing
        to use. We cannot promise it will always be online, always load, or
        always be correct, and we are not responsible for what happens if you
        rely on something here that turns out to be out of date. Anything that
        matters, a payment deadline or a departure time, is worth confirming
        with an officer or the advisor.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="panel">
      <div class="panel-header"><h2>Changes to this page</h2></div>
      <p class="panel-body">
        We post changes here and update the date at the top. The full history is
        public in our
        <a href="https://github.com/JohnsCreekFBLA/johnscreekfbla.github.io" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub repository</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <p class="page-footnote">
      Questions: <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>
      &middot; <a href="/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a>
    </p>
  </main>
  <Footer client:load />
</body>
</html>
